# Line endings (2026-07-27).
#
# Why this file exists: without it git on Windows converted the working tree to CRLF while the
# index held LF, so `git status` reported sixteen files as modified when nothing in them had
# changed — a 3305-insertion, 3305-deletion diff that `--ignore-cr-at-eol` showed to be empty.
# Every commit then carried a page of "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings, and a real change
# was impossible to tell apart from the noise.
#
# LF everywhere, including in the working tree. This is not a preference: `scripts/verify/*.sh`
# run in Git Bash and inside the container, and a shell script with CRLF fails there with
# `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`. The Dockerfile, the compose file and everything under src/ end
# up in a Linux container too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The exceptions, and the reason for each.
# PowerShell and batch files are run by Windows tooling, which wants CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.mcpb binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
